From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: Preserve natural presentation completion across queued commands.

GRANDIA II can call Start(VT_EMPTY) on an already started session between
MEEndOfPresentation and the final stream-sink marker. Command submission
clears SESSION_FLAG_PRESENTATION_ENDING, and the sink-driven EOF path does
not restore it. The ensuing automatic stop emits MESessionStopped instead
of MESessionEnded. This was observed after the resurrection movie
movies/magic/m05.mp4, with the session stopped and its lock free. Correcting
this event alone does not resolve the game's wait; 0059 also serializes the
replay requested from its MEEndOfPresentation handler.

Set the ending flag when the fully drained presentation begins its internal
stop. This also covers the synthesized-EOP path where the media source did
not send MEEndOfPresentation. Defer clearing the flag for an external command
until that command actually executes, so queuing a command during the
asynchronous sink/source stop cannot change its completion event. Explicit
Stop commands still clear the flag before starting their own transition.

Follow-up to the sink-driven EOF handling in 0003. Keep the sample-grabber
callback lock fix in 0024; this is a separate completion-event failure.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/739
References:
 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/medfound/mesessionended
 https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/medfound/mesessionstopped
diff --git a/dlls/mf/session.c b/dlls/mf/session.c
index 32ab0719..de79aa33 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -492,7 +492,6 @@ static HRESULT session_submit_command(struct media_session *session, struct sess
     EnterCriticalSection(&session->cs);
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr = session_is_shut_down(session)))
     {
-        session->presentation.flags &= ~SESSION_FLAG_PRESENTATION_ENDING;
         if (list_empty(&session->commands) && session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_COMPLETE)
         {
             hr = MFPutWorkItem(MFASYNC_CALLBACK_QUEUE_STANDARD, &session->commands_callback, &op->IUnknown_iface);
@@ -2857,6 +2856,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI session_commands_callback_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface,
     assert( session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_SUBMITTED );
     list_remove(&op->entry);
 
+    /* Queuing a command must not change the reason for an in-progress stop. */
+    session->presentation.flags &= ~SESSION_FLAG_PRESENTATION_ENDING;
+
     switch (op->command)
     {
         case SESSION_CMD_CLEAR_TOPOLOGIES:
@@ -4424,6 +4426,8 @@ static void session_sink_stream_scrub_complete(struct media_session *session, IM
     if (session->presentation.flags & SESSION_FLAG_SOURCES_SUBSCRIBED &&
             session_nodes_is_mask_set(session, MF_TOPOLOGY_OUTPUT_NODE, TOPO_NODE_SCRUB_SAMPLE_COMPLETE))
     {
+    /* A command may have cleared the ending flag while the sinks were draining. */
+    session->presentation.flags |= SESSION_FLAG_PRESENTATION_ENDING;
         IMFMediaEventQueue_QueueEventParamVar(session->event_queue, MESessionScrubSampleComplete, &GUID_NULL, S_OK, NULL);
         session_nodes_unset_mask(session, MF_TOPOLOGY_OUTPUT_NODE, TOPO_NODE_SCRUB_SAMPLE_COMPLETE);
     }
